  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Start Fund - Nigeria Alert 676 - Anticipation of Electoral Violence</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&quot;In the build -up to the 2023 general elections in a few weeks, the political space has been heated up with ongoing campaigns across the presidential candidates and agitations from their supporters virtually, across social media platforms, and with physical encounters some of which have turned violent     The impact could result in loss of lives and properties, loss of livelihoods for those affected and displacement in extreme cases. People are often caught up in conflict as they start and escalate rather rapidly without measures in place to mitigate, minimise impact or provide immediate relief  We are unable to access funding to prepare for preventive, immediate, and interim response to this potential crisis within this time. However, the availability of the Start Fund will enable us to set preventive steps to enable prompt identification of early warning signs of sudden and escalating election violence to enable an early response and mitigation measures towards curtailing the violence.</narrative>
  </description>
